# Regular (isotropic) acoustic fluid domain (type 'F') -- reference for the
# isotropic-equivalent sanity check of the anisotropic-density domain (type 'A').
# Same Vp and Rho as mater.in: the FluidAniso constant case builds
# rho^{-1}_ij = (1/rho) delta_ij and kappa = rho*Vp^2, so both domains must
# produce identical seismograms (up to machine precision).
# Format: type Vp Vs Rho Qp Qmu
1
F 1500.0 0.0 1000.0 0.0 0.0
